===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|tetrarchia|lang=la}} from Ancient Greek {{term|τετραρχία|tr=tetrarkhia|lang=grc}}, from {{term|tetra||four}} + {{term|archos||ruler}} + ''[[-ia]]'', literally "four rulers".

===Noun===
{{en-noun|tetrarchies}}

# Historically, an empire that was ruled by four rulers.

